<h2 class="mt-12">Customer acquisition matchup FAQ</h2>
<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6">
<div><h3>Klaviyo or Shopify Email for customer acquisition?</h3><p>Start customer acquisition on Shopify Email while sends stay occasional and catalogs compact; Klaviyo pays when customer acquisition branching and reporting complexity arrives — forecast profile cost on customer acquisition list growth.</p></div>
<div><h3>Omnisend vs Klaviyo for customer acquisition?</h3><p>Customer Acquisition speed favors Omnisend for lean crews; customer acquisition depth favors Klaviyo as logic matures. Run the same customer acquisition journey live on both and compare maintenance hours.</p></div>
<div><h3>Mailchimp or Klaviyo for customer acquisition?</h3><p>For customer acquisition, Mailchimp fits editor-comfortable newsletter teams; Klaviyo fits event-driven customer acquisition on Shopify orders, carts, and browse — check official pricing pages for both at your customer acquisition volume.</p></div>
<div><h3>Do I need a separate SMS tool for customer acquisition?</h3><p>Hold specialist SMS for customer acquisition until texts demonstrably move customer acquisition numbers; platform-bundled SMS covers the start — with customer acquisition consent, quiet hours, and unit pricing confirmed.</p></div>
<div><h3>How should I suppress audiences in customer acquisition flows?</h3><p>Guard customer acquisition with exits for buyers, open cases, refunds, and no-consent profiles, auditable per customer acquisition flow. In customer acquisition, a suppression miss hurts worse than a missed blast.</p></div>
<div><h3>What does customer acquisition email cost?</h3><p>Costs combine the platform subscription, contact or send overages, SMS credits, template and creative work, and the discount budget your customer acquisition campaigns consume. For customer acquisition budgeting, treat any static quote as stale — check official pricing pages and model an eighteen-month total before committing.</p></div>
<div><h3>Which app should a lean team pilot first for customer acquisition?</h3><p>For customer acquisition, choose whatever the team masters in a fortnight — native email for plain customer acquisition sends, a lean ESP once customer acquisition branching matters. A finished customer acquisition pilot beats a stalled grand plan.</p></div>
<div><h3>How do I measure customer acquisition email results?</h3><p>For customer acquisition reporting, pair attributed revenue with margin per send, repeat purchase, unsubscribe/complaint rates, and support load — then validate against a customer acquisition holdout so peak-season demand is not credited to the flows.</p></div>
<div><h3>Can I run customer acquisition email without an agency?</h3><p>Yes, if the scope stays small. Pick one customer acquisition journey, document consent and suppression rules, and reuse a simple template system. Bring outside help onto customer acquisition only when flow complexity, deliverability repair, or peak-season customer acquisition volume outruns in-house capacity.</p></div>
<div><h3>When should I graduate from my first app for customer acquisition?</h3><p>Move off the starter customer acquisition setup when flow edits feel risky, purchase-state segments for customer acquisition misfire, or contact growth makes cost unpredictable. For customer acquisition, that moment usually arrives when more than two people maintain flows or when peak campaigns require documented suppression.</p></div>
<div><h3>How much discounting is acceptable for customer acquisition?</h3><p>Treat discounts as one lever, not the default. For customer acquisition, test content-led recovery and loyalty first, cap discount depth against margin, and document who can approve exceptions. When customer acquisition revenue only converts with a code attached, suspect customer acquisition value communication before blaming price points.</p></div>
<div><h3>Which Shopify data matters most for customer acquisition?</h3><p>Order and refund state, cart and browse events, consent source, and product availability cover most customer acquisition decisions. On customer acquisition, prove events in a test checkout before trusting them in flows, with customer acquisition field definitions written where both teams can find them.</p></div>
<div><h3>How do I avoid duplicate sends across apps for customer acquisition?</h3><p>Give one platform ownership of each customer acquisition journey, document which app sends what, and share suppression lists where the tools support it. Peak-season customer acquisition hygiene means a weekly sample audit — customers pulled at random, every customer acquisition message they received listed.</p></div>
<div><h3>What should a customer acquisition pilot include?</h3><p>Run customer acquisition as a contained test: one audience, a journey or two, suppression in writing, holdout measurement, and a thirty-day customer acquisition check on margin and complaints against criteria set pre-launch.</p></div>
</section>
